=== Simulation → Compare: Graphs / Evaluate tabs ===

Context:
Compare page gets two OntoBricks tabs. "Graphs" keeps the existing overlay canvas and Comparison Setup unchanged. "Evaluate" asks one prompt of the Graph Chat agent twice, against the live graph and against the selected scenario sandbox, and shows both replies side by side (plain readonly text areas, no diff). Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-05-compare-evaluate-tab-design.md.

1. src/front/templates/partials/simulation/_sim_compare.html: wrapped in canonical card-integrated page-tabs structure (`card h-100` > `card-body p-0 ob-tabs-wrap` > `nav nav-tabs ob-tabs nav-fill`, with standard `section-header ... mb-4`), matching Workbench and Settings. Graphs pane keeps every existing `simCompare*` id. New Evaluate pane: prompt, "Ask both" button, hint, and two columns (Live / Sandbox) with spinner, inline error, and readonly output.
2. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-evaluate.js (new): SimulationEvaluate. Runs both Graph Chat turns in parallel via POST /dtwin/assistant/chat with history [] and persist false. Live uses the Comparison Setup source; Sandbox uses inferred plus the scenario id. Per-side loading/error/ok states, stale-run guard, Ctrl/Cmd+Enter to submit.
3. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-compare.js: `_toggleRun()` also refreshes the Evaluate Ask button (shared scenario picker).
4. src/front/static/simulation/css/simulation.css: tab panes fill the section height; `.sim-eval-output` min height, no resize.
5. src/front/templates/simulation.html: loads simulation-evaluate.js.
6. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py: `POST /dtwin/assistant/chat` accepts optional `persist` (default true). When false, saved domain history is not read and the exchange is not written to the session cache. Write-back extracted to `_chat_record_turn` to keep `dtwin_assistant_chat` within the size budget. Streaming route unchanged.
7. tests/units/api/test_dtwin_chat_persist_flag.py (new): persist false ignores saved history and writes nothing; default still persists and uses saved history.
8. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py: contracts for the tab skeleton, Evaluate pane ids, graphs ids kept, stateless Graph Chat payloads, script include, and CSS hook.

